EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: Traefik 3.6.7 adds a 10s handshake timeout and post-handshake connection close in the ACME TLS-ALPN path — assumption A1 is refuted

TARGET_IMAGE: traefik:v3.6.7
TARGET_PORT: 443/tcp
CLIENT_TOOL: custom TLS client (raw socket, ClientHello with acme-tls/1 ALPN, no handshake completion)

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Opened 500 TCP connections to traefik:v3.6.7 each sending a ClientHello with
  acme-tls/1 in the ALPN extension, then stopped responding. Each connection was
  closed by Traefik after approximately 10 seconds (the read deadline introduced in
  3.6.7). Goroutine count and FD count remained bounded. No legitimate HTTPS requests
  were blocked. The 10s rotation pivot was also mitigated: connections freed after
  10s regardless of attacker action. Fix: commit e9f3089, Traefik 3.6.7 (January 2026,
  CVE-2026-22045).
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 ("no timeout in ACME TLS-ALPN handler") is refuted.
                Traefik 3.6.7 adds SetDeadline(10s) for both read and write in the
                ACME TLS-ALPN path in pkg/server/router/tcp/router.go, and closes
                the connection after the handshake completes or fails.
